    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "64591d73_b0ba8506",
        "filename": "poly1305/poly1305_arm.s",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 221,
      "author": {
        "id": 5935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-08-18T01:58:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After copying the 8 bytes to the stack, it also loads into g and R11.\nSo, at line 226, g and R11 have *(R1) and *(R+4) respectively.\n\nFor line 231, yes I think line 231 and line 236 should be changed as well. I couldn\u0027t catch it since LDR with unaligned access is handled by breaking the memory access down into multiple memory accesses in ARM v6 and v7. (I couldn\u0027t test it with v5 since I don\u0027t have it.)\nhttp://www.heyrick.co.uk/armwiki/Unaligned_data_access\n\nI\u0027ll update line 231 and 236.\n\n(BTW if we can support only v6 or above, we can simply use LDR instead of LDM for unaligned case. But I\u0027m not sure whether we can do that.)",
      "parentUuid": "64591d73_157fe31c",
      "revId": "02ec784e5e29b4ec912c1d8e8d36c860ecb8bf93",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
